Consider an allocation rule $f = (f_i)_{i=1}^N$, where
    $f_i: \mathbb{R}^N \times \mathbb{R}^N \times \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}_+$. We call $f$
    \emph{shortfall-minimizing} if it satisfies the following property: 
    \begin{equation}
      s \geq \sum_{i=1}^N (\xi_i - x_i)_+ \implies
    f_{i}(\bm{x}, \bm{\xi}, s) \geq \xi_i -   x_{i}, \;\; \text{for all $i \in [N]$},
      \label{eq:allocation-rule-property}
    \end{equation}
